  concept: "Authored objective: Storage charged with observed rise.\nAuthored requirement:
    Capacitor rises at least 0.30 V and reaches 4.10 V. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction
    required.\nGeneral teaching principle: Capacitor voltage and current vary with
    circuit state; transient observations need a stated time and reference.\nOnly
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A storage tank illustrates temporary storage, but electrical capacitance
    has precise circuit equations.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A transient reading is not automatically a settled reading.
